# Controller Integration Tests

Every `@RestController` (and any Spring MVC `@Controller` that exposes HTTP APIs) **must** have Spring Boot integration tests that exercise the real web layer against the application's configured stack.

## Required pattern

Use **PostgreSQL and RabbitMQ Testcontainers** (via Spring Boot `@ServiceConnection`) so ITs do not depend on developer-local infrastructure. Prefer the shared base / config already in the project (`AbstractControllerIT`, `TestcontainersConfiguration`). Do **not** introduce H2 for controller ITs.

```java
// ✅ GOOD — full context + MockMvc against PostgreSQL + RabbitMQ Testcontainers
// Spring Boot 4: org.springframework.boot.webmvc.test.autoconfigure.AutoConfigureMockMvc
// Spring Boot 4: org.springframework.boot.testcontainers.service.connection.ServiceConnection
@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureMockMvc
@Import(TestcontainersConfiguration.class)
@Transactional // rollback so seed data is not permanently polluted
class CompanyControllerIT {

  @Autowired MockMvc mockMvc;

  @Test
  void createCompany_returnsCreated() throws Exception {
    mockMvc.perform(post("/api/companies")
            .header("X-User-Id", "1")
            .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
            .content("""
                {"name":"IT Co","state":"CA","useRegisteredAgentService":false}
                """))
        .andExpect(status().isCreated());
  }
}

// ❌ BAD — slice test only; does not satisfy full Spring Boot integration requirement alone
@WebMvcTest(CompanyController.class)
class CompanyControllerWebMvcTest { /* ... */ }

// ❌ BAD — H2 instead of Postgres Testcontainer
@SpringBootTest
@TestPropertySource(properties = "spring.datasource.url=jdbc:h2:mem:test")
class CompanyControllerIT { /* ... */ }

// ❌ BAD — assumes manually started local Postgres/RabbitMQ without Testcontainers
@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureMockMvc
class CompanyControllerIT { /* hits localhost by default */ }
```

## Coverage expectations

When adding or changing a controller endpoint:

1. Add or update an integration test under `src/test/java/...` (name `*IT` or `*IntegrationTest`).
2. Hit the HTTP path with `MockMvc` (or `TestRestTemplate` if the project standardizes on it)—not only direct service calls.
3. Assert status codes and key response fields; cover happy path and important error cases (validation, not found, business rules) when applicable.
4. Prefer `@Transactional` rollback or explicit cleanup of rows created by the test; do not permanently destroy Flyway seed data.
5. Flyway migrations (including V1 seed users/agents) must run against the Testcontainer; tests may rely on that seed.
6. Domain events that publish on transaction commit will **not** fire under `@Transactional` test rollback — use a dedicated non-rollback IT (e.g. `DomainEventNotificationIT`) when asserting messaging side effects.

## Prerequisites

Docker must be available for Testcontainers to start PostgreSQL and RabbitMQ.

## Scope

This rule applies when editing controllers or their integration tests. Service-layer unit tests with Mockito do **not** satisfy this requirement.
